-- ============================================================================
--  EcoGreen Group CRM — complete database setup
--  Generated from supabase/migrations/*.sql — do not edit this file by hand.
--  Regenerate with:  npm run sql:bundle
--
--  HOW TO RUN IT
--  1. Supabase dashboard → SQL Editor → New query
--  2. Paste this whole file
--  3. Run
--
--  It takes a few seconds and is safe to run once on an empty project. It is
--  NOT idempotent — running it twice on the same project will error on the
--  first `create type`. If you need to start over, run this first:
--      drop schema public cascade; create schema public;
--      drop schema private cascade;
--
--  WHAT IT CREATES
--  · 40 tables across tenancy, pipeline, quoting, operations, money,
--    messaging, audit and compliance
--  · Row Level Security on every one of them, deny-by-default
--  · Helper functions in a `private` schema, kept out of the RLS graph so
--    policies cannot recurse
--  · Server-side transactions for lead intake, booking, the scheduler,
--    job sheets and GDPR export/erasure
--  · Seed data: 6 brands, 8 branches, 36 services, the item catalogue,
--    36 rate cards, retention policies and 8 message sequences
--
--  BEFORE YOU QUOTE A REAL CUSTOMER
--  Every seeded rate card carries `provisional = true`. Those numbers are
--  recommendations, not this business's prices — see DECISIONS.md §2.
--  Congestion and ULEZ are seeded at zero rather than guessed.
-- ============================================================================
